{
  "_comment": "Per-formula overrides for brew-changes' changelog resolution. `url` is a manual override for formulae whose real changelog isn't reachable through GitHub auto-detection: most aren't GitHub-native (GNU/GNOME/language runtimes/etc, pointed at their own site or a self-hosted git). A few (pnpm, gemini-cli) DO have real GitHub repos with real Releases, but Homebrew's homepage/url fields don't reference GitHub, so ghsource.ResolveRepo can't find them automatically; those point straight at the repo's /releases page. Verified reachable (HTTP 200) as of 2026-08-07; re-verify periodically since upstream projects reorganize docs. `lax_headings` opts a formula whose changelog file IS found via normal GitHub auto-detection into a looser version-heading match: some files (tmux's CHANGES, xz's NEWS) mark version sections with plain, unmarked lines rather than Markdown ATX/Setext headings, which the default strict matcher can't locate.",
